I will pay him, uh, $10,000!

00:46:43.780 --> 00:46:46.280
Well, even $10,000's better than nothing.

00:46:47.290 --> 00:46:49.490
Where can I find this Laszlo Laszlo?

00:46:49.490 --> 00:46:52.750
I don't know, he disappeared after he made this record!

00:46:52.750 --> 00:46:55.060
And nobody's seen or heard of him since!

00:46:55.060 --> 00:46:56.760
He must be someplace!

00:46:56.760 --> 00:47:00.000
And I, good and bad, will find him!

00:47:01.790 --> 00:47:03.590
So long, pal, and good luck.

00:47:05.570 --> 00:47:07.230
Okay, men, you know the set-up.

00:47:07.530 --> 00:47:11.210
We're droppin' Operation Penny in favor of Operation Lazlo Lazlo.

00:47:11.390 --> 00:47:15.610
If we find him before Good and Bad does, it'll be worth 10,000 bucks to us.

00:47:15.790 --> 00:47:18.330
I want you guys to spread out and mingle with the neighborhood.

00:47:18.630 --> 00:47:21.610
Mingle, mingle, mingle, knock on doors and ask for Lazlo.

00:47:21.870 --> 00:47:26.240
Now hurry, get goin' and bring back Lazlo Lazlo.

00:47:27.160 --> 00:47:29.340
Excuse, please, may I say something?

00:47:29.340 --> 00:47:29.760
Huh?

00:47:30.090 --> 00:47:32.790
Oh, you again, can't you see I'm busy, boy?

00:47:32.790 --> 00:47:33.970
All right, remember, gang,

00:47:33.970 --> 00:47:36.370
be on the lookout for good violin music.

00:47:36.370 --> 00:47:38.330
Okay, okay, will you leave a little dust?

00:47:38.330 --> 00:47:39.670
We like it that way.

00:47:39.670 --> 00:47:40.670
- Excuse, please.

00:47:40.670 --> 00:47:41.870
- Now, don't tell me, I know.

00:47:41.870 --> 00:47:43.310
You're cleaning up, ha-ha!

00:47:43.310 --> 00:47:45.480
- I heard you say something about violin music.

00:47:45.480 --> 00:47:46.880
- You? Very funny.

00:47:46.880 --> 00:47:49.980
First he's trying out for comedy and now violin music.

00:47:49.980 --> 00:47:52.520
Ah-ha-ha, Carnegie Hall, I suppose.

00:47:52.520 --> 00:47:53.960
- I thought perhaps I could help.

00:47:53.960 --> 00:47:56.200
- Look, you got a good broom there and you're good with it.

00:47:56.200 --> 00:47:57.700
Stick to that, we'll manage.

00:47:57.700 --> 00:48:00.000
Come on, Benny, we gotta knock on doors.

00:48:00.000 --> 00:48:04.150
Wait a minute. I don't want to see that again.

00:48:04.150 --> 00:48:06.200
Okay, Benny, let's go.

00:48:06.200 --> 00:48:11.960
The violin, they throw it away.

00:48:11.960 --> 00:48:15.640
We'll start with the building across the street.

00:48:15.640 --> 00:48:17.410
Come on, Benny, we got the light.

00:48:17.410 --> 00:48:19.410
If we find that Laszlo, Laszlo,

00:48:19.410 --> 00:48:21.710
we'll raise the price to 15,000.

00:48:23.930 --> 00:48:25.530
Oh, boy, that music again.

00:48:25.530 --> 00:48:28.340
I wish Dibble would knock it off with that record.

00:48:28.340 --> 00:48:30.000
It isn't Dibble's record.

00:48:30.060 --> 00:48:33.060
It's a street cleaner. He's playing my violin.

00:48:33.060 --> 00:48:36.060
A street cleaner? I thought I told him to stick to his broom.

00:48:36.060 --> 00:48:39.060
A street cleaner?

00:48:39.060 --> 00:48:53.660
Let's get him! For all we know, he could be...

00:48:53.660 --> 00:48:57.680
Stop the music! I mean, stop the car!

00:49:00.120 --> 00:49:08.110
Come on, Benny, let's go. That street cleaner must be Laszlo Laszlo.

00:49:08.110 --> 00:49:12.260
Uh-oh, the light. What a time for the light.

00:49:12.260 --> 00:49:16.380
The street cleaner's talking to Mr. Goodenbad, T.C.

00:49:16.380 --> 00:49:21.410
Hey, we saw him first. Don't sign, Laszlo, baby. Don't sign.

00:49:21.410 --> 00:49:27.060
Sue, we'll take this to the highest court.

00:49:27.060 --> 00:49:30.000
What's with this light? Come on, change it.

00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:40.600
We got the light! Hold it! Don't go! Wait, good and bad, Lazlo, wait!

00:49:40.600 --> 00:50:00.000
I've been robbed! Sick, sick, sick! Here he was, right under my nose. I'm cleaning up, he says. A real comic. Can I help you with the violin music, he says. No, thanks. We can manage. Stick to your broom, I say. I don't think I'll help you with the violin music, he says.

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:02.560
Monaghy Hall is ready for you yet. Unquote.

00:50:03.080 --> 00:50:03.720
I blew it.

00:50:04.280 --> 00:50:06.740
10,000 bucks waiting and I blew it.

00:50:06.860 --> 00:50:08.720
I blew it. I blew it. I blew it.

00:50:10.130 --> 00:50:12.940
Hey, wait a minute.

00:50:15.840 --> 00:50:22.840
Benny, is that you playing?

00:50:23.360 --> 00:50:25.060
You sound just like Bora Minovitch.

00:50:25.370 --> 00:50:26.920
He makes a fortune with her monikers.

00:50:27.140 --> 00:50:28.390
Wait a minute, what did I say? A fortune?

00:50:28.630 --> 00:50:30.000
Bora Minovitch. Benny...

00:50:30.060 --> 00:50:33.040
Are you sure it's you playing that thing? There is no record some place.

00:50:33.040 --> 00:50:35.440
Oh, it's me, all right, T.C.

00:50:35.440 --> 00:50:38.010
I've been playing the harmonica all my life.

00:50:38.010 --> 00:50:39.900
Why? Do you like it?

00:50:39.900 --> 00:50:42.670
Like it? It's great! We'll clean up!

00:50:42.670 --> 00:50:46.200
Taxi! Play, Benny, play. Maybe we can still catch good and bad.

00:50:46.200 --> 00:50:48.110
Taxi! Taxi!

00:50:48.110 --> 00:50:52.010
We'll make records. Maybe you can get your own TV program.

00:50:52.010 --> 00:50:53.170
Taxi!

00:50:53.170 --> 00:50:55.390
Personal appearances, concerts, guest shots.

00:50:55.390 --> 00:50:57.590
Keep playing, Benny. Don't lose it. Keep playing.

00:50:57.590 --> 00:50:59.920
Taxi! Taxi!
